   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "fCg0i0TNW3Id"
   },
   "source": [
    "Observations:\n",
    "1. Missing values make up 7.76% of all cells and affect 19.2% of the pages. They are concentrated at the start of the window.\n",
    "2. 20,088 pages have leading NaNs (series starts late) and 652 pages have no data at all.\n",
    "\n",
    "Treatment:\n",
    "1. Will drop the 652 pages that are 100% NaN, since they carry no information.\n",
    "2. Interpolate interior gaps linearly, page by page.\n",
    "3. Fill leading/trailing NaNs with the nearest observed value.\n",
    "\n",
    "Why not choosing the other alternatives:\n",
    "- Fill with 0: the language average would rise over time only because more pages \"appear\", which creates a false upward trend.\n",
    "- Fill with the mean: page sizes range from 0 to millions of views, so one mean ignores each page's scale and its own time pattern.\n",
    "- Drop pages with any NaN: this removes 19.2% of the pages."
   ]
  },
